# Data: clean images, depth maps, segmentation labels, generated fog outputs.
# clean/ and segmentation/ are symlinks into local Cityscapes downloads
# (machine-specific paths, recreated by scripts/setup_data.py); depth/ and
# generated/ are regenerable via scripts/extract_depth.py, generate_*.py.
# All of it is too large/derived to belong in git.
#
# NOTE: these are per-subdirectory (not a blanket `data/`) so that
# data/fid_calibration/image_manifest.json can still be tracked below --
# git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is itself excluded,
# so a blanket parent exclusion + `!` negation for one file does NOT work.
data/clean/
data/depth/
data/segmentation/
data/generated/
data/evaluation/
# FID calibration writes ~500 regenerable PNGs per sweep into per-variant
# subdirectories here; the manifest JSON (which 50 images + beta_base per
# image) sits directly in data/fid_calibration/ and is deliberately NOT
# matched by this directory-only pattern.
data/fid_calibration/*/

# Results: comparison figures, diffs — regenerable via scripts/*comparison*.py.
# results/metrics/ is deliberately not ignored: it only ever holds small
# CSV/JSON summaries (e.g. FID calibration results) worth tracking.
results/comparisons/

# Third-party clone (HazeFlow), has its own git history. Re-clone via:
#   git clone https://github.com/cloor/HazeFlow.git external/HazeFlow
external/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# OS cruft
.DS_Store

# Local Claude Code runtime state (not project content)
.claude/

# Numpy arrays (depth caches, etc.)
*.npy

# Model weights / checkpoints
*.pth
*.pt
*.ckpt
*.safetensors
*.h5
*.onnx
*.bin
